Wait, HUD bottom position absolute inside `.hud` which has `padding`; absolute positioning uses the padding box? Absolute children are positioned relative to the padding box edges? Actually relative to the padding box (content + padding) of the containing block. `.hud` is position absolute with inset 0, so its padding box includes padding. left:12px within the padding box? The containing block for an absolutely positioned descendant is the padding box of the ancestor. So left/right/bottom relative to the padding edge. The `.hud` padding is 12/24; using left 12 right 12 bottom 132 relative to padding box maybe weird. Better set `.hud-bottom { position: relative; }`? Hmm, to reposition, easiest: use flex layout: keep hud-bottom in flow but add margin-bottom: 120px via body.touch-mode .hud-bottom { margin-bottom: 118px; }. Since .hud is flex column with justify-content space-between, hud-bottom at bottom with margin-bottom pushes it up. That works and respects padding. Use:
```
body.touch-mode .hud-bottom { margin-bottom: 116px; }
```
